      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Atchison, Topeka and Santa Fi Railway began in 1859 with Atchison as its eastern terminus, linking Kansas to the southwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atchison%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Atchison houses the World’s Smallest Presidential Library, a quirky tribute to “President Atchison” inside the historic Santa Fe Depot Museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
